{% extends "base.html" %}{% block title %}Scripted — backup-engine{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<section class="screen read" aria-label="Scripted destination setup">
  <p class="eyebrow">Setup · destination · scripted</p>
  <h1>Scripted setup</h1>
  <p class="lead">Run this from a shell that already has your AWS <strong>admin</strong>
     credentials (<code>AWS_PROFILE</code> or <code>AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</code> /
     <code>AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</code>). Admin creds stay in your shell — this container
     never sees them.</p>

  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-4)">You need the repo checked out on a machine
     with <code>aws</code> and <code>tofu</code> (OpenTofu) installed, and admin credentials
     active in that shell. A good bucket name is <code>unraid-backup-&lt;your-account-id&gt;</code>
     to match the automated mode.</p>

  <p class="slabel" style="margin-top:var(--sp-5)">Run this</p>
  <div class="cmd" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2)">
    <pre>./setup.sh &lt;bucket-name&gt; &lt;region&gt;</pre>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm copy" data-copy="./setup.sh <bucket-name> <region>">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-3)">It wraps <code>tofu apply</code> — creating
     the bucket, a least-privilege IAM user and the bucket-admin role — and prints the runtime
     key/secret plus the <code>backup.env</code> lines (region, bucket, the two role/policy ARNs
     and <code>PERMISSIONS_VERSION</code>). Keep the checkout: re-running it later updates the
     AWS permissions in place.</p>

  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-5)">Then paste the printed key/secret into
     <a class="linklike" href="{{ url_for('gui.provision_manual') }}">guided-manual → Test &amp; Validate</a>,
     or straight into <a class="linklike" href="{{ url_for('gui.config_page') }}">Keys &amp; secrets</a>.
     Test &amp; Validate finishes on AWS permissions, where Verify confirms the rest. Then set the
     recovery passphrase and create your first job.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
